# Shell scripts must always have LF line endings, regardless of the
# checking-out machine's git config (core.autocrlf) — a CRLF shell script
# baked into a Linux Docker image fails with "bad interpreter" (the
# shebang line's trailing \r isn't part of a valid interpreter path).
# Found live while adding docker/postgres/10-init-app-role.sh (Phase 15,
# docs/ASSUMPTIONS.md) on this Windows dev machine.
*.sh text eol=lf
